          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Finding: work order identified; late-event determination is blocked\n\nThe September order ending in **1070** is **MO-25-09-1070**, work order **WO-2025-09-004**, for a **Cooler Plate Pack** at Modine’s Racine operation.\n\n| Requested item | Verified result |\n|---|---|\n| Cost period | **Sep-25 — PER-COST-2025-09** |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Relevant source transaction | Not available in the readable records |\n| Event amount | Not verifiable |\n| Exact event-created time | Not verifiable |\n| Minutes after Pending Close | Not calculable without the event-created time |\n| Recorded accounting status | Not verifiable |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | **Undetermined** |\n\nThe Pending Close timestamp is reproduced exactly; the source supplies no timezone or UTC offset.\n\n### Evidence limitation\nThe accessible records contain work orders and cost periods, but **no cost-event rows**. Supporting records were not staged, and the corresponding dataset package denied access. Consequently, I cannot establish whether a late event occurred. **This is not evidence that no late event occurred.**\n\n### Oracle’s documented treatment\nOracle’s *Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting* section states that newly created transactions falling in or before a Pending Close period are not staged in Cost Accounting or Receipt Accounting and are processed after the period is closed or reopened. Transactions entered before Pending Close continue processing. **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions** that continue processing.\n\nTherefore, a newly created, non-exempt September manufacturing transaction after **2025-09-30T18:00:00** should be held from processing while the period remains Pending Close. Without the event’s type, creation time, and recorded status, an event-specific consistency conclusion would be unsupported.\n\n*Sources: supplied `work_orders` and `cost_periods` records; Oracle 26B policy PDF, PDF page 233 / printed page 225.*\n\nNo database records were changed. The incomplete audit was submitted as **needs evidence** and saved to `/cache/work/worker_466ef8887637/audit-report.json`.",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
